From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:19:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: horizon_run --report-json and aot_report.py, the
 numbers of a run as a file (#14)

horizon_run.py --report-json FILE writes, when the run ends (and with --build-only, the static part only), the
survey of the build (survey.classify: lifted, replaced, left to the JIT, by reason and mnemonic) and every counter of
the runtime (jit_entries, jit_to_aot, fallback_requests, jit_invalidations, unlifted_calls...), with the share of
native functions and of indirect transfers the AOT table could not take. aot_report.py shows one report and
compares two. Tested without a game: the arithmetic, the file, the text, the option, and a fixture module whose
function Remill cannot lift (N calls, N entries into the JIT, and a --build-only run through the real command).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A run of a recompiled game writes its AOT and JIT figures to a file, so that two runs can be compared
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#14

